# Non Euclidean Game

## Big Picture
- 2d game that players can move around in and collect points
- hyperbolic (maybe spherical?) geometry

## Steps
- [x] create gui
    - [x] player class (KeyListener)
    - [x] tile class (different colors, uses GridGame code)
    - [x] wasd player movement
    - [x] paint the player on top of the tiles
    - [x] create euclidean tiles (squares)
- [ ] translate euclidean square tiles into hyperbolic
    - [x] make the tiles trapezoids
    - [x] make the tiles "on a tube"
      - [x] add horizontal shrinking to the horizons
    - [x] use hyperbolic formula ((x, y) = (tanh(r/2)/2)(x, y))
    - [x] player movement consistent with hyperbolic space
    - [x] player stays in the center as the map moves
- [ ] other improvements
    - [ ] make player face the correct direction
- [ ] add goals
    - [ ] world exploration - add different objects
    - [ ] things to pick up? enemies?
    - [ ] point tracking
    - [ ] timed?